# RBIN Task Flow (Cursor)

**Task flow** = **RBIN Task Flow**. Data lives in `.task-flow/` — never edit `.internal/` by hand.

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `.task-flow/tasks.input.txt` | Define tasks (`- description`) |
| `.task-flow/tasks.status.md` | Progress (auto) |
| `.task-flow/.internal/tasks.json` | Definitions |
| `.task-flow/.internal/status.json` | Status source of truth |
| `.task-flow/contexts/` | Specs / mockups |
| `.task-flow/dev-logs/` | Manual steps + conversation log (`task-X.Y-manual.md`) |
| `.task-flow/guides/` | Platform guides, Graphify, standards, reports |

## Prefer skills (`.cursor/skills/`)

| User intent | Invoke |
|-------------|--------|
| `task-flow: sync` | `@task-flow-sync` or [task-flow-sync.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/task-flow-sync.mdc) |
| `task-flow: from contexts` | `@task-flow-from-contexts` |
| `task-flow: run next X`, `run N` | `@task-flow-run` |
| `task-flow: run-split:N` | `@task-flow-run-split` |
| `task-flow: status` | `@task-flow-status` |
| `task-flow: audit` | `@task-flow-audit` |
| `task-flow: validate` | `@task-flow-validate` |
| `task-flow: estimate X` / `X,Y` / `all` | `@task-flow-estimate` |
| `task-flow: report X` | `@task-flow-report` |
| Implementing code | the `coding_standards.mdc` checklist |
| Suggest commit | a Conventional Commit (policy: `rbin-git-policy.mdc`) |

Natural language (`work on next 3 subtasks`) = same as `task-flow: run next 3`.

**Manual subtasks:** user reports progress in chat; AI updates `.task-flow/dev-logs/` Conversation log and marks `done` when verified — no separate command.

## Git (always)

Never write git — user runs all commits. Policy: [rbin-git-policy.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/rbin-git-policy.mdc). Suggest via a Conventional Commit (policy: `rbin-git-policy.mdc`).

## Graphify (optional)

On `run` / `validate`, if `graphify-out/` exists: `graphify query` before repo-wide grep. Rule: `graphify-task-flow`. Guide: `.task-flow/guides/GRAPHIFY.md`.

